/name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>If a conventional cell of the type in which an organic monomeric compound is provided in the space between the anode and cathode is heated, the liquid organic monomeric compound seeps out from the space, heightening the possibility of abnormality such as ignition. A cell according to the invention is free from the above problem. A cell element comprises an anode (1), a cathode (2), and an ion conduction layer (3) formed between the electrodes and impregnated with an electrolyte containing an organic monomeric compound. An absorbing substance (4) for absorbing the organic monomeric compound is provided around the cell body. The cell element and the absorbing substance (4) are contained in a package (5).</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Lorsqu'une cellule conventionnelle du type comportant un composé organique monomère entre l'anode et la cathode est chauffée, ledit composé organique liquide peut suinter, ce qui rend plus probables des anomalies telle que l'inflammation. L'invention concerne une cellule ne présentant pas ce problème et comprenant une anode (1), une cathode (2) et une couche de conduction ionique (3) formée entre les électrodes et imprégnée d'un électrolyte contenant un composé organique monomère. Une substance absorbante (4), destinée à absorber ledit composé organique, entoure le corps de la cellule. Un boîtier renferme (5) l'élément cellule et la substance absorbante (4).</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set fo